28.     OFSTED MONITORING VISITS
28.1. Where the Customer is made aware that OFSTED has assessed the Supplier as having made “insufficient
       progress” after a monitoring visit, the Customer may, at its absolute discretion take one or more of the
       following actions:
        28.1.1       require the Supplier to accept and comply with additional contractual obligations relating
                     to the improvement of the Services assessed as insufficient progress;
        28.1.2 reduce and / or recover from the Supplier Contract Charges paid by the Customer in respect of
                   that part of the Services that has been assessed as having made insufficient progress;
        28.1.3       suspend the payment of Contract Charges for current Learners for a specified period;
        28.1.4       not consider any applications or pay any Contract Charges for new Learners for a specified
                     period;
